      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Make one revision",
        "body": "**Make one deliberate revision**\n\nRead your graph. Change one venue fact, then ask the AI to revise the decision and next step to match. Review the transaction, apply it, and check that the connections still make sense.\n\n**You have a first graph**\n\nYou can find your question, explain a labeled connection, and identify the next step.\n\n**Keep it**\n\nThe graph is in your browser until you save it. Choose Save in the File menu. Saving is the part of Twilite you pay for: the editor, a monthly subscription. Everything on screen comes with you through sign-in and payment, and then you choose where it goes: a repository of yours on GitHub, or a file. Reading and sharing graphs stay free. [Get the editor](https://twilite.zone/?get-editor=1)",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-bootstrap-llm"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
    },
